## Two evaluation libraries disagree on identical structured answers

Source: TestMu AI — https://www.testmuai.com/blog/langsmith-vs-braintrust/
Published: 2026-10-25
Channel: news

Evaluation scorers turn an AI system’s answers into results that engineers compare across releases. TestMu AI’s October 25 comparison of LangSmith and Braintrust includes an original test of their associated open-source scoring libraries. It reports different exact-match outcomes on seven of twenty identical input pairs. The test ran October 19; October 25 is the article’s publication date.

For example, two JSON objects containing the same keys and values in different orders failed autoevals’ exact-match check but passed openevals’. A team migrating its evaluation code could therefore see a score change even when its agent produced the same answer. That operational implication is editorial guidance, not a measured deployment outcome.

The published run used autoevals 0.4.0 and openevals 0.2.0 without model judges. This small, vendor-published comparison does not establish either platform’s overall quality, and this edition has not independently rerun it.

Why it matters: For evaluation owners: test scorer migrations against fixed examples before interpreting score changes as model improvements.

