## Phoenix refreshes MiniMax model choices while preserving custom IDs

Source: Arize AI / Phoenix — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/arize-phoenix-v20.26.1
Published: 2026-10-25
Channel: github

Phoenix is an open-source platform for examining AI traces and running evaluations; its playground lets engineers try model calls. The October 25 stable release updates the MiniMax text-model catalog. The linked change places MiniMax-M3.1-Flash first and MiniMax-M3 second, replacing an older suggested preset.

The change preserves the provider-default fallback so saved and custom model identifiers still resolve. For illustration, an engineer comparing a saved configuration with a newly selected preset should record the actual model identifier used for each run. A refreshed menu alone does not establish that two runs used equivalent settings, or that one model performs better.

The release’s linked pull request describes tests covering catalog order, model inference, custom identifiers and both regional endpoints. These are maintainer-reported checks, not tests rerun by this edition. The release also adds Microsoft Agent Framework tracing documentation; that is documentation for an existing integration, not evidence that tracing support first became available on October 25.

Why it matters: For Phoenix playground users: check the selected MiniMax model identifier before comparing new runs with saved results.

